    <string name="onboarding_vendor_title">%1$s phones need one more step</string>
    <string name="onboarding_open_autostart">Open autostart settings</string>
    <string name="onboarding_storage_title">How should Wasl reach your files?</string>
    <string name="onboarding_storage_body">Either way, it only syncs folders you pair.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_storage_all_files_body">Browse any folder from inside Wasl, Download included. Android shows a switch to turn on.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_storage_one_folder_title">One folder at a time</string>
    <string name="onboarding_storage_one_folder_body">Use Android\'s folder picker for each pair. Some folders, like Download, can\'t be picked this way.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_storage_android_data">Android never lets apps sync Android/data or Android/obb, whichever you choose.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step_of">Step %1$d of %2$d</string>
    <string name="onboarding_vendor_xiaomi">MIUI and HyperOS stop background apps unless Autostart is on and battery saver is set to \"No restrictions\". Security app → Manage apps → Wasl → turn on Autostart; then Battery saver → No restrictions. Also lock the app in Recents (pull it down and tap the lock).</string>
    <string name="onboarding_vendor_huawei">EMUI and Magic UI close apps that are not set to \"Manage manually\". Settings → Apps → App launch → Wasl → turn off automatic management, then enable Auto-launch, Secondary launch and Run in background.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_vendor_samsung">One UI puts unused apps to sleep. Settings → Battery → Background usage limits → make sure Wasl is not in \"Sleeping apps\" or \"Deep sleeping apps\" and add it to \"Never sleeping apps\". If syncs still stall, turn off \"Put unused apps to sleep\" and Adaptive battery.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_vendor_oppo">ColorOS and Realme UI block background work unless auto-launch is allowed. Settings → Apps → Wasl → allow Auto launch; then Battery → Allow background activity. Also lock the app in Recents.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_vendor_vivo">Funtouch OS and OriginOS need background auto-start and high background power use allowed. i Manager → App manager → Autostart manager → enable Wasl; Settings → Battery → Background power consumption management → allow Wasl.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_vendor_oneplus">OxygenOS optimizes battery aggressively. Settings → Battery → Battery optimization → Wasl → Don\'t optimize; and Settings → Apps → Wasl → Battery usage → Allow background activity. Turn off \"Sleep standby optimization\" if present.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_vendor_asus">Mobile Manager can stop background apps. Mobile Manager → PowerMaster → Auto-start manager → allow Wasl, and turn off \"Clean up in suspend\" and \"Deny auto-start of apps\".</string>
    <string name="onboarding_vendor_lenovo">Some Lenovo and Motorola models ship a background app manager that closes apps. Settings → Battery → Battery optimization → Wasl → Don\'t optimize, and check for a \"Background apps\" or \"Power manager\" entry in Settings.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_vendor_nothing">Nothing OS is close to stock Android; the standard battery optimization exemption is normally enough. If syncs still stall: Settings → Apps → Wasl → Battery → Unrestricted.</string>

